## Why This Is Asked

Tests for REST accuracy and real-time streams, plus cross-service consistency, are critical for user-facing product data. This question probes end-to-end reliability under realistic failures and multi-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end testing of REST + streaming APIs
- Data consistency between REST state and streaming deltas
- Reconnect/backoff handling for WebSocket streams
- Per-tenant isolation and security controls
- Failure modes: downstream cache and search index outages
- Tooling for orchestration, mocks, and load testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node-like test sketch (using ws and axios)
const axios = require('axios');
const WebSocket = require('ws');

async function testProductSync(productId, tenantKey) {
  const rest = await axios.get(`https://api.example.com/products/${productId}`, {
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${tenantKey}` }
  });
  const ws = new WebSocket(`wss://api.example.com/ws/products/updates?productId=${productId}`, {
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${tenantKey}` }
  });
  // Simplified: compare first REST payload with first delta, then on each delta
  // close sockets, simulate reconnection delays, etc.
}
```

