## Why This Is Asked
Tests reliability of composite APIs with dependent services.

## Key Concepts
- Downstream latency, timeouts, partial failures, circuit breakers
- Idempotent retries, exponential backoff, observability
- End-to-end timing and schema validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test using jest + nock
const nock = require('nock');
const request = require('supertest');
const app = require('../app');
test('partial data when one downstream times out', async () => {
  nock('http://sales').get('/daily').delay(3000).reply(200, {sales: 1000});
  nock('http://customers').get('/daily').reply(200, {customers: 50});
  const res = await request(app).get('/reports/daily');
  expect(res.statusCode).toBe(200);
  expect(res.body).toHaveProperty('sales');
  expect(res.headers).toHaveProperty('x-downstream-warn');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test circuit-breaker behavior under sustained latency?
- What metrics would you validate in your observability stack?

